00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:47.830
How do you do, Riri?

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:50.290
Miss Yuyu.

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.950
Everyone.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:56.120
Here, Riri. This is for you.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:02.500
This is...

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:07.700
Come on. Don't just stare at it; put it on.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:10.910
Where did you find this on sale?

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.200
It looks just like the one I lost.

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:18.250
It <i>looks </i>like it?!

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.790
Isn't it the same one?

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:23.410
My four-leaf clover had a crack in one leaf.

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:25.580
This one doesn't, so...

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:28.620
I should have done more research.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:31.080
What do you mean by that, Kaede?

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:36.540
O-Oh, Miss Yuyu, you look positively terrifying.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.160
What's this?

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.620
This...

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:45.450
This is mine!

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:47.870
There are two of Riri's hair tie?

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:50.910
Kaede made the new one herself.

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:52.330
Shiori?!

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:54.200
What's going on?

00:15:56.370 --> 00:16:01.330
I found the real one on the
beach on the second or third day.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:04.000
But in the state it's in,

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:07.620
I thought it would just make Riri sadder.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:10.750
So, the one we found today is...?

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:16.620
I knew a search that large was
bound to find where the real one was,

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.540
so I got up early and moved it.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.160
To think you duped us, too.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:25.500
So, I picked it up before anyone else

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.910
and switched it with
the fake I finished last night.

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:34.250
I'm amazed you put so much effort into it.

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:36.160
Yes, all right, I did it!

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:39.910
It's an inescapable fact that
I tricked Riri and all of you!

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:42.870
You may punish me however you see fit.

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:47.700
Now the cat's out of the bag,
all the blame should fall on me!

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.330
You got Shiori totally involved.

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:53.750
No, I just let her use the workshop.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:57.450
I had no idea what she
was making until just now.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.580
Kaede.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:05.250
Wh-What?

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.290
You're all right.

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:08.290
Yup.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:09.450
Huh?

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:19.410
Thank you, Kaede.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:23.160
Y-You're welcome.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:26.200
And thank you, everyone.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:30.290
Kaede was probably right.

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:36.330
If I only had this one, I'd only be
able to remember the painful things.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:39.290
But with this one to go with it,

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:44.330
I can tell how all of you feel and be happy.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:47.910
They're both real to me.

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.250
I-I see.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:54.080
Then, uh, I guess that means everything
went according to plan, right?

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:59.700
Stand up. I'm going to thank you, too.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.950
Thank you, Kaede.

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:05.700
You don't have to. I did it for Riri.

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:09.410
There's no need for you
to thank me, too, Miss Yuyu.

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:13.700
I'm speaking as her Schutzengel...
as her big sister.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:16.450
Oh, I know what this is.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:21.500
You're trying to tell me, "Riri's mine,
and you can't have her," aren't you?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.620
Yes, exactly.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.580
So, you admit it!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:28.870
Give up. You fought well.

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:39.040
Huh?

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.700
I wonder why?

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:45.200
I'm happy, so why...?

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:57.330
Go ahead and cry, Riri.

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:00.000
What you need right now

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:04.500
is to let your feelings out, whatever they are.

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:08.120
I wasn't able to protect her!

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.040
Yuri.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.580
Even though I was supposed to take care of her!

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.290
You did all you could.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:27.250
No one could have prevented what happened.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:44.950
Now, where should I begin?

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.000
Just the gist.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:50.120
I'll make this as quick as I can, then.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.540
The formulae on this Dáinsleif

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:55.540
have been overwritten by someone.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:03.250
It's conceivable that these formulae
influenced the Huge in some way.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:06.580
Influenced a Huge through a CHARM?

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:09.540
Is such a thing possible?

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:12.330
I don't know the details yet.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:18.000
But given that Lilies and Huge have
Magie in common, they share a root.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:21.450
You could say they have
a strong natural affinity.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:26.370
This Dáinsleif belonged to Shirai, did it not?

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:32.910
Yes, but the last person
to make a pact with it was...

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.410
Kawazoe, then.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:37.830
Yes.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:42.160
The last person to hold this
CHARM before it was recovered

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:45.160
was Yuyu's then-Schutzengel,

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:47.830
Miss Kawazoe Misuzu.

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:30.200
I'm finally able to come visit.

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:34.830
Umm...

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:40.160
Should we pay our respects to Miss Misuzu, too?

00:22:42.910 --> 00:22:44.580
Let's.

00:22:47.750 --> 00:22:49.450
Yuyu,

00:22:49.450 --> 00:22:53.330
how did you get over what
happened to Miss Misuzu?

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:54.660
I don't know.

00:22:54.660 --> 00:23:00.080
But you have to accept what happened over time.

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:04.500
There's no way to change the past.

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:07.540
I think it will take me a long time.

00:23:07.540 --> 00:23:10.290
That's fine.

00:23:10.290 --> 00:23:13.370
The cruelest thing about a person's death

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:18.700
is that it cuts off everyone connected to them.

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:23.790
Their thoughts, wishes, and feelings

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:28.330
are frozen in time, forever unfinished.

00:23:28.330 --> 00:23:34.790
All the people left behind can do is wonder.

00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:36.580
Well said.

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:41.500
You mustn't make your precious Schild worry.

00:23:42.910 --> 00:23:45.700
Even if they're a ghost,

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:49.870
if we could share our feelings
with the real person again,

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:53.080
maybe that could be a kind of comfort.

00:23:57.450 --> 00:24:00.910
But you're...

00:24:03.910 --> 00:24:06.910
"To be continued"

00:24:06.910 --> 00:24:07.750
"Next time"
"Episode 11"

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:10.500
"Next time"
"Episode 11"

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:10.500
So, you're Riri.

00:24:10.500 --> 00:24:11.950
"Next time"
"Episode 11"

00:24:10.500 --> 00:24:11.950
Nice to meet you.

00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:12.540
"Illustration: Ditama Bow"

00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:12.540
Nice to meet you.

00:24:12.540 --> 00:24:16.870
"Illustration: Ditama Bow"
